  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. Innovative ideas for enhancing data visualization tools using AI were solicited by July 20th. The project reached a significant milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. A prototype for secure file sharing was also successfully tested, with UI enhancements planned for October. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. The executive board approved a total budget of $2M for all phases, and a separate $15,000 budget was approved for training programs starting next month."
